From db2b5b65476e8d83851222a69310dcbf7107285d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:40:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: avoid every shop entrance that is not the goal shop

When flowing to a shop, the Borg is meant to keep off the entrances of
the other shops, since stepping onto one enters it. The test skipped such
an entrance only when it was in neither the Borg's row nor its column
(y != row && x != column), so an entrance in line with the Borg stayed on
the path and the Borg walked into the wrong shop. Skip every other shop
entrance except the grid the Borg stands on.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#125.

(cherry picked from commit 9d35babe8bd8e38b2d522e00ce159d740919718f)
---
 src/borg/borg-flow.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-flow.c b/src/borg/borg-flow.c
index 56ee66f5d..b0c2151cd 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-flow.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-flow.c
@@ -412,8 +412,8 @@ void borg_flow_spread(int depth, bool optimize, bool avoid, bool tunneling,
 
             /* Avoid shop entry points if I am not heading to that shop */
             if (borg.goal.shop >= 0 && feat_is_shop(ag->feat)
-                && (ag->store != borg.goal.shop) && y != borg.c.y
-                && x != borg.c.x)
+                && (ag->store != borg.goal.shop)
+                && (y != borg.c.y || x != borg.c.x))
                 continue;
 
             /* Avoid Traps if low level-- unless brave */
-- 
